From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:04:04 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] soc: qcom: connect IPQ6018 secure WCSS and SMP2P acknowledgments

The IPQ6018 WCSS firmware is loaded through the secure PIL remoteproc
driver. Describe the remote processor with its secure PIL compatible and
provide the firmware name used to locate the WCSS firmware. Enable the
QDSS_AT clock required while loading that firmware.

IPQ6018 has a AHB based Q6v5 802.11ax radios that are supported by the
ath11k.

IPQ6018 seem to need different ack mechanism for smp2p messaging. This
fixes q6v5_wcss remoteproc firmware reloading. Without this first load is
OK, but subsequent loads would hang and fail to complete.

Merged from:
  0905-arm64-dts-qcom-ipq6018-use-secure-WCSS-remoteproc.patch
  0906-arm64-dts-qcom-ipq6018-add-wifi-node.patch
  0907-soc-qcom-fix-smp2p-ack-on-ipq6018.patch

Based on work by:
  Mantas Pucka <mantas@8devices.com>
  Robert Marko <robimarko@gmail.com>

